l}},"districts":{"list":[],"translations":{}},"zones":{"list":[20],"translations":{"de":["Norden"],"pt":[null],"en":["North"],"it":["Nord"],"cn":[null],"fr":["Nord"],"sp":["Norte"],"nl":["Noord"]}},"neca":null,"facebook_id":null,"backoffice_id":40661,"location":{"lat":50.8623729,"lon":4.40129256},"region":"brussels","import_origin":null,"external_id":null,"is_in_address_book":false,"is_in_vb_export":false,"resto_ranking":0},"organizer":{"last_updated_at":"2024-01-10T10:43:38+01:00","published_at":"2013-10-19T01:13:28+02:00","id":106651,"translations":{"de":{"name":"Botanischer Garten Jean Massart (ULB)","address_street_name":"Chauss\u00e9e de Wavre","address_street_number":"1850","address_street_box":null,"email":"jardmass@ulb.be","website":"http:\/\/www.ulb.be\/actulb\/dds\/jmassart\/","phone_contact":"+32 2 650 91 65","phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1160","address_city":"Auderghem","address_line1":"Chauss\u00e9e de Wavre, 1850","address_line2":"1160 Auderghem","description_web":"Der Botanische Garten Jean Massart wurde 1922 von dem gro\u00dfen Natursch\u00fctzer und Botanik-Professor an der Freien Universit\u00e4t Br\u00fcssel Jean Massart gegr\u00fcndet. Er befindet sich in Auderghem, ganz in der N\u00e4he der historischen Klosteranlage Rouge-Cl\u00f4itre, dem Soignes-Wald und den Parks Seny, Ten Reuken und Bergoje.\r\n\r\nAngelegt wurde der botanische Garten von dem Landschaftsarchitekten Jules Buyssens. Mit seinen rund 2000 Pflanzenarten z\u00e4hlt er zu den artenreichsten botanischen G\u00e4rten Belgiens. Bewundern k\u00f6nnen Sie sowohl einheimische als auch exotische Pflanzen, die hier von G\u00e4rtnern, Forschern und Studenten gehegt und gepflegt werden, denn der Garten dient als eine Art Freiluftlabor, in dem die positiven Effekte von Pflanzen in der Stadt erforscht wird. Zudem dient er als Museum der Freien Universit\u00e4t Br\u00fcssel und ist Teil des Wissenschaftsparcours, zu dem auch das Zoologische Museum geh\u00f6rt.","description_print":null,"booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null,"visit_url":null},"pt":{"name":"Jardin botanique Jean Massart (ULB)","address_street_name":"Chauss\u00e9e de Wavre","address_street_number":"1850","address_street_box":null,"email":"jardmass@ulb.be","website":"https:\/\/sciences.brussels\/massart\/","phone_contact":"+32 2 650 91 65","phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1160","address_city":"Auderghem","address_line1":"Chauss\u00e9e de Wavre, 1850","address_line2":"1160 Auderghem","description_web":null,"description_print":null,"booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null,"visit_url":null},"en":{"name":"Jean Massart Botanical Garden (ULB)","address_street_name":"Waversesteenweg","address_street_number":"1850","address_street_box":null,"email":"jardmass@ulb.be","website":"http:\/\/www.ulb.be\/actulb\/dds\/jmassart\/","phone_contact":"+32 2 650 91 65","phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1160","address_city":"Auderghem","address_line1":"Waversesteenweg, 1850","address_line2":"1160 Auderghem","description_web":"Named after its founder, the Jean Massart Botanical Garden was created in 1922 by this great defender of nature and professor of botany at the ULB (Free University of Brussels). It's located in Auderghem, a stone's throw from Rouge-Clo\u00eetre, the Sonian Forest and the Seny, Ten Reuken and Bergoje parks.\r\n\r\nThis botanical garden was designed by landscape architect Jules Buyssens. With some 2,000 plant species, it's one of the richest botanical gardens in Belgium and a real living museum. Admire the thousands of native and exotic plants that the gardeners, researchers and students take care of every day. The garden is an open-air laboratory for studying how plants can make cities healthier and more sustainable. It's also a museum of ULB and is part of the science trail, together with the Museum of Zoology.","description_print":null,"booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null,"visit_url":null},"it":{"name":"Jardin botanique Jean Massart (ULB)","address_street_name":"Chauss\u00e9e de Wavre","address_street_number":"1850","address_street_box":null,"email":"jardmass@ulb.be","website":"https:\/\/sciences.brussels\/massart\/","phone_contact":"+32 2 650 91 65","phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1160","address_city":"Auderghem","address_line1":"Chauss\u00e9e de Wavre, 1850","address_line2":"1160 Auderghem","description_web":null,"description_print":null,"booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null,"visit_url":null},"cn":{"name":"Jardin botanique Jean Massart (ULB)","address_street_name":"Chauss\u00e9e de Wavre","address_street_number":"1850","address_street_box":null,"email":"jardmass@ulb.be","website":"https:\/\/sciences.brussels\/massart\/","phone_contact":"+32 2 650 91 65","phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1160","address_city":"Auderghem","address_line1":"Chauss\u00e9e de Wavre, 1850","address_line2":"1160 Auderghem","description_web":null,"description_print":null,"booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null,"visit_url":null},"fr":{"name":"Jardin botanique Jean Massart (ULB)","address_street_name":"Chauss\u00e9e de Wavre","address_street_number":"1850","address_street_box":null,"email":"jardmass@ulb.be","website":"https:\/\/sciences.brussels\/massart\/","phone_contact":"+32 2 650 91 65","phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1160","address_city":"Auderghem","address_line1":"Chauss\u00e9e de Wavre, 1850","address_line2":"1160 Auderghem","description_web":"Du nom de son fondateur, le jardin botanique Jean Massart a \u00e9t\u00e9 cr\u00e9\u00e9 en 1922 par ce grand d\u00e9fenseur de la nature et professeur de botanique \u00e0 l\u2019Universit\u00e9 Libre de Bruxelles. Il est situ\u00e9 \u00e0 Auderghem, \u00e0 deux pas du Rouge-Clo\u00eetre, de la for\u00eat de Soignes et des parcs Seny, Ten Reuken et du Bergoje.\n\nCe Jardin botanique a \u00e9t\u00e9 dessin\u00e9 par l\u2019architecte paysagiste Jules Buyssens. Avec ses quelque 2000 esp\u00e8ces v\u00e9g\u00e9tales, il est l\u2019un des plus riches jardins botaniques de Belgique et un v\u00e9ritable mus\u00e9e vivant. Admirez-y les milliers de plantes indig\u00e8nes et exotiques dont les jardiniers, chercheurs et \u00e9tudiants prennent soin quotidiennement. Le Jardin est un hotspot de biodiversit\u00e9, outre le r\u00e8gne v\u00e9g\u00e9tal, il accueille une diversit\u00e9 exceptionnelle d'animaux et surtout d'insectes avec plus de 4000 esp\u00e8ces r\u00e9pertori\u00e9es. Il est d\u2019ailleurs un mus\u00e9e de l\u2019Universit\u00e9 Libre de Bruxelles et fait partie du parcours des sciences, avec notamment le Mus\u00e9um de Zoologie.","description_print":"Cr\u00e9\u00e9 en 1922, le Jardin botanique Jean Massart est g\u00e9r\u00e9 par Bruxelles Environnement en collaboration avec l\u2019Universit\u00e9 Libre de Bruxelles.\r\nLe public peut y d\u00e9couvrir un v\u00e9ritable mus\u00e9e vivant de plein air comprenant plus  de 2000 esp\u00e8ces v\u00e9g\u00e9tales dont plusieurs centaines sont \u00e9tiquet\u00e9es.\r\nDestin\u00e9es \u00e0 la recherche, \u00e0 l\u2019enseignement universitaire et \u00e0 la vulgarisation,  les diverses collections qui le composent  se r\u00e9partissent sur 5 hectares en bordure de for\u00eat de Soignes.\r\n\r\nQue peut-on y voir ?\r\n\r\nDans la zone humide, \u00e9tang et marais abritent de nombreuses plantes typiques de notre r\u00e9gion.  \r\nUne collection impressionnante de plantes m\u00e9dicinales permet de rappeler l\u2019importance des plantes en th\u00e9rapeutique. Un verger regroupe d\u2019anciennes vari\u00e9t\u00e9s de pommiers et poiriers. L\u2019arboretum rassemble divers conif\u00e8res et d\u2019autres arbres non indig\u00e8nes.\r\nLes principales familles botaniques de plantes \u00e0 fleurs sont illustr\u00e9es dans le Jardin \u00e9volutif. Une collection de plantes cultiv\u00e9es rassemble plusieurs esp\u00e8ces domestiqu\u00e9es par l\u2019homme ainsi que leurs anc\u00eatres sauvages.\r\nEnfin, les plantes exotiques envahissantes et les plantes m\u00e9tallicoles, deux th\u00e9matiques \u00e9tudi\u00e9es au Laboratoire d\u2019Ecologie v\u00e9g\u00e9tale et Biog\u00e9ochimie, ont \u00e9galement leur parcelle de d\u00e9monstration.\r\n\r\nCe site particuli\u00e8rement riche et diversifi\u00e9 est class\u00e9 depuis 1997. \r\nIl est accessible gratuitement du lundi au vendredi de 9h00 \u00e0 17h00.\r\nDes visites guid\u00e9es sont propos\u00e9es tous les jeudis et 2\u00e8me samedi du mois (de mai \u00e0 fin octobre) ou sur rendez-vous pour les groupes (\u00e9coles, associations\u2026)\r\nhttp:\/\/www.ulb.ac.be\/musees\/jmassart \r\n","booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null,"visit_url":null},"sp":{"name":"Jard\u00edn bot\u00e1nico Jean Massart (ULB)","address_street_name":"Chauss\u00e9e de Wavre","address_street_number":"1850","address_street_box":null,"email":"jardmass@ulb.be","website":"http:\/\/www.ulb.be\/actulb\/dds\/jmassart\/","phone_contact":"+32 2 650 91 65","phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1160","address_city":"Auderghem","address_line1":"Chauss\u00e9e de Wavre, 1850","address_line2":"1160 Auderghem","description_web":"Las ex\u00f3ticas colecciones vivientes del jard\u00edn bot\u00e1nico, creado en 1922 por Jean Massart, fueron creadas para la investigaci\u00f3n, la ense\u00f1anza universitaria y la promoci\u00f3n cient\u00edfica.\r\nPosee casi 2000 especies vegetales localizadas en 5 hect\u00e1reas y divididas en diferentes jardines: el jard\u00edn medicinal y plantas arom\u00e1ticas, el jard\u00edn bot\u00e1nico experimental, el jard\u00edn de plantas cultivadas, un huerto, un invernadero y un \u00e1rea experimental. Tambi\u00e9n puedes encontrar dos colecciones asociadas a dos estudios llevados a cabo por la ULB: vegetaci\u00f3n metalofita y plantas invasivas.\r\nTambi\u00e9n hay una \u00e1rea h\u00fameda establecida como reserva natural e inclu\u00edda en la Red Natura 2000.","description_print":null,"booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null,"visit_url":null},"nl":{"name":"Botanische tuin Jean Massart (ULB)","address_street_name":"Waversesteenweg","address_street_number":"1850","address_street_box":null,"email":"jardmass@ulb.be","website":"http:\/\/www.ulb.be\/actulb\/dds\/jmassart\/","phone_contact":"+32 2 650 91 65","phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1160","address_city":"Oudergem","address_line1":"Waversesteenweg, 1850","address_line2":"1160 Oudergem","description_web":"Jean Massart was professor plantkunde aan de Universit\u00e9 Libre de Bruxelles. Hij was een fervent natuurliefhebber. In 1922 riep hij de tuin in Oudergem in het leven. De tuin ligt op een steenworp van het Roodklooster, het Zoni\u00ebnwoud en van het Seny-, het Tenreuken- en het Bergojepark.\r\n\r\nHet ontwerp komt van landschapsarchitect Jules Buyssens. Met ongeveer 2.000 plantensoorten is het een van de rijkste botanische tuinen van Belgi\u00eb. Hier waan je je in een levend museum. Elke dag worden de duizenden inheemse en exotische planten verzorgd door tuiniers, onderzoekers en studenten. De tuin is dan ook een openluchtlaboratorium. Hoe kunnen planten steden gezonder en duurzamer maken? Dat s de vraag waarover ze zich hier buigen. De tuin is ook een museum van de Universit\u00e9 Libre de Bruxelles en maakt deel uit van het wetenschapsparcours, samen met het Museum voor Dierkunde.","description_print":null,"booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null,"visit_url":null}},"neca":null,"facebook_id":null,"region":"brussels","backoffice_id":369,"location":{"lat":50.8142056,"lon":4.4388072},"is_in_address_book":true,"is_in_vb_export":true,"import_origin":null,"external_id":null,"resto_ranking":0},"media":[{"type":"photo","link":"https:\/\/agendabrussels2.imgix.net\/883532cde85dde42621ab969acdf32decabbc1bb.jpg","width":2560,"height":1704,"ratio":1.5,"oEmbed_height":1704,"oEmbed_width":2560,"translations":{"de":{"title":"Visite guid\u00e9e : D\u00e9couverte des collections botaniques","copyright":null},"pt":{"title":"Visite guid\u00e9e : D\u00e9couverte des collections botaniques","copyright":null},"en":{"title":"Visite guid\u00e9e : D\u00e9couverte des collections botaniques","copyright":null},"it":{"title":"Visite guid\u00e9e : D\u00e9couverte des collections botaniques","copyright":null},"cn":{"title":"Visite guid\u00e9e : D\u00e9couverte des collections botaniques","copyright":null},"fr":{"title":"Visite guid\u00e9e : D\u00e9couverte des collections botaniques","copyright":null},"sp":{"title":"Visite guid\u00e9e : D\u00e9couverte des collections botaniques","copyright":null},"nl":{"title":"Visite guid\u00e9e : D\u00e9couverte des collections botaniques","copyright":null}}}],"dates":[{"day":"2024-05-25","doors":null,"start":"14:30:00","end":"16:00:00","end_night_life":null,"is_soldout":false,"is_canceled":false},{"day":"2024-06-08","doors":null,"start":"14:30:00","end":"16:00:00","end_night_life":null,"is_soldout":false,"is_canceled":false}],"prices":[{"translations":{"de":{"name":"Normal"},"en":{"name":"Normal"},"it":{"name":"Normale"},"fr":{"name":"Normal"},"sp":{"name":"Normal"},"nl":{"name":"Normaal"}},"value":3},{"translations":{"de":{"name":"Kinder"},"en":{"name":"Children"},"it":{"name":"Bambini"},"fr":{"name":"Enfants"},"sp":{"name":"Ni\u00f1os"},"nl":{"name":"Kinderen"}},"value":0}],"date_exceptions":[],"closing_days":[],"child_events":[],"parent_events":[],"accessibilities":[],"recurring":[],"targets":{"list":[],"translations":{}},"educational_targets":{"list":[],"translations":{}},"tags":["exterior"]},{"id":50009307,"date_start":"2024-05-17","date_end":"2024-06-15","date_next":"2024-05-25","accept_article27":false,"accept_cultuurbon":false,"accept_paspartoe":false,"is_closed_on_public_holidays":false,"is_closed_on_school_holidays":false,"is_only_by_appointment":false,"is_permanent":false,"is_free":false,"is_pay_as_you_can":false,"is_online":false,"is_canceled":false,"is_soldout":false,"last_updated_at":"2024-05-25T02:01:09+02:00","published_at":"2024-04-05T12:12:02+02:00","publication_state":"public","date_embargo":null,"show_in_agenda":true,"is_outside":false,"is_high_capacity":false,"is_not_major_event":false,"backoffice_id":297941,"facebook_link":null,"import_origin":null,"is_part_of":null,"sub_type":"expo","ranking":0.4054801330382267,"languages":{"spoken":["en","fr"],"subtitles":[]},"categories":{"main":{"id":23,"translations":{"de":"Ausstellung","pt":null,"en":"Exhibition","it":"Esposizioni","cn":null,"fr":"Exposition","sp":"Exhibici\u00f3n","nl":"Tentoonstellingen"}},"others":{"list":[24],"translations":{"de":["Kunstgalerien"],"pt":[null],"en":["Art Galleries"],"it":["Gallerie d'arte"],"cn":[null],"fr":["Galeries d'art"],"sp":["Galer\u00edas de arte"],"nl":["Galeries"]}}},"translations":{"de":{"name":"\"Le bois des r\u00eaves\" by Emilie Danchin","shortdescr":null,"longdescr":null,"performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":"http:\/\/www.thepalmbeach.be","email":"hello@thepalmbeach.be","phone_contact":"+32 474 86 42 45","phone_booking":"+32 474 86 42 45","agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/de\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.50009307"},"pt":{"name":"\"Le bois des r\u00eaves\" by Emilie Danchin","shortdescr":null,"longdescr":null,"performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":"http:\/\/www.thepalmbeach.be","email":"hello@thepalmbeach.be","phone_contact":"+32 474 86 42 45","phone_booking":"+32 474 86 42 45","agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/pt\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.50009307"},"en":{"name":"\"Le bois des r\u00eaves\" by Emilie Danchin","shortdescr":"She tackles the question of origins in a foreign place in a paradoxical way. It substitutes a space that no longer exists, which represents her origins.","longdescr":"Emilie Danchin conveys questions in her work pertaining to the realism of photography by involving the body in the pho- tographic space. It is very vibrant as well as an organic ad- venture. Emilie Danchin does not photograph reality as such, but a kind of dream rooted in the subject, to a certain extent a somewhat inhabited or animated dreamy reality. To this effect, the photographic act extends to a personal phenome- nology and the progressive creation of a visual language ca- pable of relaying a personal experience charged with images and emotions that, universally recognisable, are likely to stir viewers\u2019 feelings, disrupt thought and trigger dreams.\nEmilie Danchin introduces here Le Bois des R\u00eaves, the culmi- nation of a performance and photographic work achieved in a property that is noteworthy in terms of its architecture, as well as its gardens, in the Arts-and-Crafts style. This heritage site lent itself to her proposal to have the freedom to take over a space and a body, hers in this case. She tackles the question of origins in a foreign place in a paradoxical way. It substitutes a space that no longer exists, which represents her origins.\nThis property conjured up, through a combination of me- mories, her own English place of birth, the houses belonging to her grandmothers, their gardens in the countryside and seaside, baths, woodworks, smells, clothes, furniture, musica- lity... a whole atmosphere that is generally, culturally familiar to her. And at the same time, it recalled absence, missing people, invasion and emptiness of the body and a house that until recently remained within the same family, loss and the parentage that was interrupted.\nBy means of self-portrait, Emilie Danchin wondered what the inside of the house would look like. How would the emotions generated by the exterior of the house be conveyed in her outside landscapes? How would she extri- cate her body from the matter to render it in a landscape having similar characteristics? How would time intervene in this memory-enhanced place where her own body, her robe and some of her clothes combined with those that belonged to three generations of women, the house, gar- den, the photographic act itself have jointly become the template for a vital identity-related fiction? Her aim was to found her hope of investing a space, materialising and filling a form of absence, the place of the origins, a kind of double of another imaginary space, distant and close, inaccessible, erased, deleted, having left the body and the house and nevertheless, inalienable yet.\nLe Bois des R\u00eaves is carried by the the artist\u2019s body postures, which has become a sensitive measure of the evocative potential of the place. Equally, the place has given live to non-material memories, the vague outlines of which could not have stood out without this inseparable staging of her body and the space. The photographic medium is presented in a variety of aspects, black and white, colour, varying formats and scales, as well as dialogue between fiction and observation. Video is added to this. Processed as stills, this lends the ensemble a form of heartbeat in real time as such of perception through gaze. This results in\nan art form in several phases, the assembly of which in its entirety impresses a circular motion in space and physically creates time. Intimating the desire to go on reconnais- sance, this photographic form espouses the volatility of space and time, emotions, dreams and the sense of self. One marvels before the representation of the memory space, whose autobiographical form is that of an absolute memory and of a dream.","performers":"Emilie Danchin introduces here Le Bois des R\u00eaves, the culmi- nation of a performance and photographic work achieved in a property that is noteworthy in terms of its architecture, as well as its gardens, in the Arts-and-Crafts style. This heritage site lent itself to her proposal to have the freedom to take over a space and a body, hers in this case. \n","boxoffice_url":null,"website":"http:\/\/www.thepalmbeach.be","email":"hello@thepalmbeach.be","phone_contact":"+32 474 86 42 45","phone_booking":"+32 474 86 42 45","agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/en\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.50009307"},"it":{"name":"\"Le bois des r\u00eaves\" by Emilie Danchin","shortdescr":null,"longdescr":null,"performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":"http:\/\/www.thepalmbeach.be","email":"hello@thepalmbeach.be","phone_contact":"+32 474 86 42 45","phone_booking":"+32 474 86 42 45","agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/it\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.50009307"},"cn":{"name":"\"Le bois des r\u00eaves\" by Emilie Danchin","shortdescr":null,"longdescr":null,"performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":"http:\/\/www.thepalmbeach.be","email":"hello@thepalmbeach.be","phone_contact":"+32 474 86 42 45","phone_booking":"+32 474 86 42 45","agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/cn\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.50009307"},"fr":{"name":"\"Le bois des r\u00eaves\" by Emilie Danchin","shortdescr":null,"longdescr":null,"performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":"http:\/\/www.thepalmbeach.be","email":"hello@thepalmbeach.be","phone_contact":"+32 474 86 42 45","phone_booking":"+32 474 86 42 45","agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/fr\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.50009307"},"sp":{"name":"\"Le bois des r\u00eaves\" by Emilie Danchin","shortdescr":null,"longdescr":null,"performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":"http:\/\/www.thepalmbeach.be","email":"hello@thepalmbeach.be","phone_contact":"+32 474 86 42 45","phone_booking":"+32 474 86 42 45","agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/sp\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.50009307"},"nl":{"name":"\"Le bois des r\u00eaves\" by Emilie Danchin","shortdescr":null,"longdescr":null,"performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":"http:\/\/www.thepalmbeach.be","email":"hello@thepalmbeach.be","phone_contact":"+32 474 86 42 45","phone_booking":"+32 474 86 42 45","agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/nl\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.50009307"}},"place":{"last_updated_at":"2023-10-04T14:15:19+02:00","published_at":"2016-05-17T09:27:10+02:00","id":265910,"translations":{"de":{"name":"The Palm Beach","address_street_name":"Rue Meyerbeer","address_street_number":"61","address_street_box":null,"email":"sandrineviumasia@me.com","website":"http:\/\/www.thepalmbeach.be","phone_contact":"+32 474 86 42 45","phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1190","address_city":"Forest","address_line1":"Rue Meyerbeer, 61","address_line2":"1190 Forest","description_web":null,"description_print":null,"booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null,"visit_url":null},"pt":{"name":"The Palm Beach","address_street_name":"Rue Meyerbeer","address_street_number":"61","address_street_box":null,"email":"sandrineviumasia@me.com","website":"http:\/\/www.thepalmbeach.be","phone_contact":"+32 474 86 42 45","phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1190","address_city":"Forest","address_line1":"Rue Meyerbeer, 61","address_line2":"1190 Forest","description_web":null,"description_print":null,"booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null,"visit_url":null},"en":{"name":"The Palm Beach","address_street_name":"Rue Meyerbeer","address_street_number":"61","address_street_box":null,"email":"sandrineviumasia@me.com","website":"http:\/\/www.thepalmbeach.be","phone_contact":"+32 474 86 42 45","phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1190","address_city":"Forest","address_line1":"Rue Meyerbeer, 61","address_line2":"1190 Forest","description_web":"The Palm Beach is an atypical gallery located in an Art Deco house designed by Joseph Diongre, the architect of the Flagey building. Sandrine Viu Masia, the curator of the place, enjoys discovering young talented artists and introducing them to the public in quality exhibitions. Particular attention is paid to welcoming the audience and making them aware of the symbiosis between the setting and the exhibited works.","description_print":"The Palm Beach or a new way to meet new Artists!","booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null,"visit_url":null},"it":{"name":"The Palm Beach","address_street_name":"Rue Meyerbeer","address_street_number":"61","address_street_box":null,"email":"sandrineviuma